508 < 1      the verify and rollback steps never run.
509 < 1   2. **Verify** — the same `bash -lc "<verify cmd>"` shape, plus `ULTRA_PUBLISH_URL=<the deployed
510 < 1      url>` in its env (the deploy step never gets this var). A `publish:verify{cmd, exit, ms, url}`
511 < 1      row is written. Exit 0 writes `publish.json` (`published` true, `rollback` null) and sets
512 < 1      `phase` to `"the pull request was merged and the app is published"`.
513 < 1   3. **Rollback** — only on a red verify, and only when the plan named a `**Rollback:**` line: the
514 < 1      same `bash -lc` shape (no extra env), a `publish:rollback{cmd, exit}` row, `publish.json`
515 < 1      (`published` false, `rollback` the rollback's `{cmd, exit}`) and `phase` set to `"the pull
516 < 1      request was merged; the live check was red and the deploy was rolled back"`. A red verify with
517 < 1      no `**Rollback:**` line skips this step and sets `phase` to `"the pull request was merged; the
518 < 1      live check was red and no rollback was named"` instead, `publish.json`'s `rollback` staying
519 < 1      `null`. Every case's `publish.json` is `publish.mjs`'s own JSON, never hand-built shell JSON.
