642 < 2   - project-find-or-create — a create whose name the hub already holds answers 200 with `created: false` (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; #978).
643 < 2   - project-by-id-only — a project NAME in an issue path is 400; every issue route takes the project id (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; CONTRACT's janitor paragraph).
644 < 2   - create-replay — the same `Idempotency-Key` with the same fields answers 200, the same uid and the ORIGINAL revision (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; #978, #993).
645 < 2   - create-fingerprint-metadata — the same key with other metadata is 409 `idempotency_mismatch`, naming the prior uid: the key is fingerprinted with the body (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; #978, #993).
646 < 2   - create-duplicate-scorer — the same title with no key is 409 `duplicate_candidates` and `force_new: true` bypasses it, scored 0.93 (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-15; #993's comment — #978's 2026-09-14 table read `200, a second issue` for that case; settled 2026-09-15 by the probe's first hand run: 409 with `force_new: true` 200, the earlier reading kept as history).
647 < 2   - link-blocks-idempotent — the same `blocks` link created twice answers 200 with the same `link.id` (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; #978).
648 < 2   - link-parent-replace — a second `parent` is 409 `parent_already_set`, and `replace: true` swaps it (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; #978, #993).
649 < 2   - link-types — the types are exactly `parent`, `blocks` and `related`; `blocked_by` is 400 (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; #979).
650 < 2   - metadata-merge-if-match — a patch merges per key under `If-Match: "rev-N"`, and a stale revision is 412 `revision_conflict` (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; #978, CONTRACT's 412 sentence).
651 < 2   - metadata-dotted-flat — `work.state` is stored as the flat key `metadata["work.state"]`, never a nested object (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-13; #810's Phase A comment, CONTRACT's janitor paragraph).
652 < 2   - claim-if-unowned — a claim on an owned issue is 409 `already_claimed` carrying `data.current_owner` (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; #979).
653 < 2   - unassign-key — `expect_owner` is 400 unexpected property; the OpenAPI names `expected_owner` (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-15; #979, #993, the OpenAPI read 2026-09-15).
654 < 2   - close-evidence-required — a `done` close whose `evidence` is empty is 400 `evidence required for reason=done`; the accepted entry types are `commit`, `pr`, `test`, `reviewed-paths` and `external`, and the engine's task closes, the boot's run close and the probe each send at least one (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-15; #1023, #1026).
655 < 2   - close-message-40 — a `done` close needs a message of 40 characters or more (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-11; run-111, CLAUDE.md's kata seams, CONTRACT's close paragraph).
656 < 2   - close-retry-protocol — a close under an `Idempotency-Key` also needs `retry_protocol: "close-v1"` (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; recorded only as a comment in `fleet/kata-client.mjs`).
657 < 2   - close-superseded-evidence — a `superseded-by` close is 400 for the evidence keys `ref`, `value` and `issue`; the accepted key is undocumented (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; #978).
658 < 2   - ready-unowned — `/ready` exists, `?unowned=true` filters it, and `?owner=` is ignored (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; #978, #979).
659 < 2   - next-no-endpoint — `GET /projects/<id>/next` is 404; there is no next endpoint on the API (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; #979, #993; settled 2026-09-15 by the probe's first hand run, `/next` 404).
660 < 2   - labels-merge — adding a label twice leaves one label (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; recorded only as a comment in `fleet/kata-client.mjs`).
661 < 2   - events-issue-uid — every event carries an `issue_uid` except `project.created`, which has none (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; #978).
662 < 2   - issue-links-shape — an issue's links read `links: [{id, type, from: {uid, short_id, …}, to: {…}}]` (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; #979).
663 < 2   - archive-actor-required — `DELETE /api/v1/projects/<id>` with no `actor` query parameter is 400 `actor: required query parameter is missing`; the query is validated before any state check (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-15; #1023, #1026).
664 < 2   - purge-ladder — a purge is 412 `confirm_required` without `X-Kata-Confirm: PURGE <name>` and 409 `project_not_archived` before `DELETE /projects/<id>?actor=<name>`, and the archive itself, carrying `?actor=`, refuses `project_has_open_issues` (re-read v0.18.0, 2026-09-30; first v0.17.2, 2026-09-14; #978, #993 — the launcher's old bump purge had never once succeeded live).
665 < 2   - events-page — `GET /projects/<id>/events?after_id=N&limit=K` answers `{reset_required, events, next_after_id}`, `next_after_id` being the last event's `event_id`: a `limit` of 2 answered 100 events, so the limit is no bound and the cursor is the whole of the walk, and an empty `events` is its end. A comment event is `type` `issue.commented` with `issue_uid`, `actor` (`impl:3@run-170`) and `payload: {comment_uid, author, body, created_at}` (v0.17.2, 2026-09-17; #1095).
666 < 2   - cli-next-unowned — hand, read by a person and not the probe: #979 read the CLI's `next` as having no `--unowned`, and `kata next --help` on the hub lists one — both readings stand (v0.17.2, 2026-09-15; #979).
667 < 2   - int-hosts-https — hand, read by a person and not the probe and readable only from a VM: every `*.int.exe.xyz` host is https, http 301s, and a followed 301 turns a POST into a GET (v0.17.2, 2026-09-11; run-110, CLAUDE.md's kata seams).
668 < 1 - **exe.dev facts (measured):** every exe.dev lobby behaviour the fleet leans on, read once and
669 < 1   written down here rather than restated from memory — the readings `node fleet/tests/probe_exe_facts.mjs`
670 < 1   takes against the lobby, one row per probe fact in the probe's own order, stamped with the digest
671 < 1   of `help all --json` because exe.dev exposes no version marker (Shelley, 2026-09-23). It is
672 < 1   re-read after any verb-drift finding and before any plan touching `fleet/launch.mjs` or
673 < 1   `fleet/lobby.mjs`; a reading that moves is one edited row, and a document or an issue comment
674 < 1   cites the row instead of repeating what it says.
676 > 1   - int-hosts-https — hand, read by a person and not the probe and readable only from a VM: every `*.int.exe.xyz` host is https, http 301s, and a followed 301 turns a POST into a GET (2026-09-11; run-110).
675 < 1   - help-all-digest — `help all --json` is JSON with a `commands` array, and its sha256 is the only version marker exe.dev exposes (lobby 92465a0aa5e0141b, 2026-09-23; first read 2026-09-23, Shelley cKAZXHW).
676 < 1   - ls-json-shape — `ls --json` is `{shared_vms, vms}`; read `.vms[]` only; rows carry `vm_name`, `ssh_dest`, `ssh_host`, `status` (lobby 92465a0aa5e0141b, 2026-09-23; first read 2026-09-03, Traps).
677 < 1   - billing-plan-json — `billing plan --json` carries `max_cpus`, `max_memory_gb`, `tier` and `plan`, the pool the launcher sizes against (lobby 92465a0aa5e0141b, 2026-09-23; first read 2026-09-05, RUNBOOK §Capacity).
678 < 1   - help-verb-flags — `help <verb>` prints an `Options:` block one flag per line, the set the doctor's verb-drift row diffs (lobby 92465a0aa5e0141b, 2026-09-23; first read 2026-09-05, fleet/doctor.mjs).
679 < 1   - error-on-stdout — a lobby error comes back on stdout with exit 1 and no envelope (lobby 92465a0aa5e0141b, 2026-09-23; first read 2026-09-03, Traps).
680 < 1   - new-no-positionals — `new` takes no positionals; a spaced `--comment` travels inside one ssh argument with its quotes intact; `--memory` under 2 GB is refused with `--memory must be at least 2 GB` (a 1 GB throwaway parked the probe's first hand run) (lobby 92465a0aa5e0141b, 2026-09-23; first read 2026-09-12, the ultraviz deploy, Traps).
681 < 1   - comment-200-bytes — the VM comment holds 200 bytes (lobby 92465a0aa5e0141b, 2026-09-23; first read 2026-09-04, Traps, `COMMENT_MAX_BYTES`).
682 < 1   - share-port-single — `share port` sets the VM's single `proxy_port` and a second call replaces it (lobby 92465a0aa5e0141b, 2026-09-23; first read 2026-09-12, Traps).
683 < 1   - tag-add-remove — `tag` adds and `tag -d` removes a tag; `tag -d` of an attached tag detaches that integration at once, not re-measured by the probe (lobby 92465a0aa5e0141b, 2026-09-23; first read 2026-09-04, Traps).
684 < 1   - cp-copies-tags — `cp` copies tags by default and `--copy-tags=false` makes a copy with none (lobby 92465a0aa5e0141b, 2026-09-23; first read 2026-09-04, Traps).
685 < 1   - rm-reserves-name — a `new` with a just-deleted name succeeds — the name is not reserved (lobby 92465a0aa5e0141b, 2026-09-23 and 2026-09-29, n=2; the 2026-09-04 Trap read "reserved for good", and both probe hand runs read the opposite). The practice stands regardless: the run number is the identity and a VM name is one incarnation, never reused.
686 < 1   - refused-verbs — `new --integration` is refused since 2026-09-11 (lobby 92465a0aa5e0141b, 2026-09-23; first read 2026-09-11, Traps, #1036). `integrations attach` is live: `integrations attach reaper tag:fleet` answered `reaper is already attached via tag:fleet`, and `help integrations` lists `attach`/`detach` and no `policy` (2026-09-30, n=1, #1434).
687 < 1 - **SDK and edge-auth facts (measured 2026-09-17, one hand-stood `--tag fleet` box):** the readings
688 < 1   the Agent SDK worker layer rests on, taken on `jev-probe-09172119` (node 24.20.0, SDK 0.3.274,
689 < 1   image CLI 2.1.272) under the boot's own engine env, one row per probe. A reading that moves is one
690 < 1   edited row; a document or an issue comment cites the row instead of repeating it.
691 < 1   - sdk-through-the-edge — `query()` with `settingSources: []` and
692 < 1     `outputFormat: {type:'json_schema'}` answers through the edge bearer under
693 < 1     `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://claude-max.int.exe.xyz`, `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=placeholder`,
694 < 1     `env -u CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`: `apiKeySource: none`, structured output honoured, 3.0 s wall, and
695 < 1     `system/init.capabilities` advertises `interrupt_receipt_v1`, `interrupt_cancel_queued_v1`,
696 < 1     `msg_lifecycle_v1` (2026-09-17; #1131 probe 1).
697 < 1   - env-only-auth — the same query answers with `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=placeholder` and NO
698 < 1     `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`, and the control with neither variable set fails fast
699 < 1     (`Not logged in · Please run /login`, `terminal_reason: api_error`, 0.5 s). Env-only auth is
700 < 1     therefore real and not the edge answering regardless, so the four-flag `--bare` substitute the
701 < 1     old engine's worker `buildArgs` carried was retirable (2026-09-17; #1131 probe 2, the 2026-08-28
702 < 1     `--bare` blocker settled).
703 < 1   - setup-token-infers-but-fails-the-bearer-probe — a `claude setup-token` one-year token installed
704 < 1     as `claude-max`'s bearer SERVES INFERENCE (same query, structured output, 2.1 s) and passes the
705 < 1     boot's first gate (`claude auth status` → `authMethod: oauth_token`, `apiProvider: firstParty`),
706 < 1     but `GET /api/oauth/usage` through the proxy is 403 `oauth_scope_insufficient`, required scope
707 < 1     `user:profile`, with a `"type":"error"` body — exactly the shape `factory/preflight.mjs`
708 < 1     classifies as a dead credential, so it would PARK EVERY RUN at boot. The token is
709 < 1     inference-scoped by construction. Retiring the four-hour refresh and the revocation trap of
710 < 1     runs 92/100/103 therefore costs one change to the bearer probe, not zero (2026-09-17; #1131
711 < 1     probe 3).
712 < 1   - doctor-reads-the-comment-not-the-token — with the setup-token installed, all eight
713 < 1     `node fleet/doctor.mjs` rows stayed ok and the accounts row named the drift itself
714 < 1     (`edge carries setup-token-probe-2026-09-17; fleet.json names marcus.e-gmail.com`): the doctor
715 < 1     reads `--comment account=<name>`, never the bearer (2026-09-17; #1131 probe 3).
716 < 1   - refresh-without-force-does-not-rotate — `node fleet/claude-token.mjs refresh --account <name>`
717 < 1     with an unexpired record reinstalls the CACHED access token at the edge and mints nothing, so it
718 < 1     is the safe way to restore the bearer; only `--force` rotates and revokes. `--account` is
719 < 1     required when the keychain account is not `ultrapowers`, or the refresh reports no refresh token
720 < 1     (2026-09-17; #1131 probe 3's rollback).
721 < 1   - fanout-no-429 — trivial structured haiku queries, all succeeding, no rate limit at any width
722 < 1     read: 1 wide 3.0 s; 10 wide 6.2 s wall, per-query median 4.4 s, 10/10, zero 429; 30 wide 13.9 s
723 < 1     wall, per-query median 10.7 s, zero 429. Latency stretches roughly linearly past 10, so the
724 < 1     bound on width is throughput and not a 429 (n = 41 queries, 2026-09-17; #1131 probe 4).
725 < 1   - maxturns-1-loses-to-thinking — three of the 30-wide queries ended `error_max_turns` /
726 < 1     `terminal_reason: max_turns` after spending ~370 thinking tokens without emitting the structured
727 < 1     answer. `maxTurns: 1` with `outputFormat` is not safe on a thinking model; it is a worker-shape
728 < 1     defect and reads as a rate limit if only the failure count is looked at (n = 3 of 30,
729 < 1     2026-09-17; #1131 probe 4).
730 < 1   - sdk-cost-is-not-a-cost-sensor — `result.total_cost_usd` under the edge proxy reported $0.0468
731 < 1     for a haiku turn of 10 input / 165 output with ~20k cache-read and ~2.6k cache-creation tokens,
732 < 1     roughly 8× a hand price of the same usage. The token counts in `result.usage` are the readable
733 < 1     quantity; the dollar figure is an estimate the subscription path does not make true
734 < 1     (2026-09-17; #1131 probe 1).
735 < 1 - **Laptop config `~/.ultrapowers/fleet.json`** — `cpu`, `memory`, `account` and `evidence`, every
736 < 1   one of them optional to the file, an unknown key ignored and a missing file meaning the defaults:
737 < 1 
738 < 1   ```json
739 < 1   {
740 < 1     "cpu": "8",
741 < 1     "memory": "16GB",
742 < 1     "account": "<name>",
743 < 1     "evidence": "<owner>/<repo>"
744 < 1   }
745 < 1   ```
746 < 1 
747 < 1   `memory` is `<int>GB` or `<int>G`; a bare number or a fractional `1.5GB` is unreadable. `account`
748 < 1   is the keychain account the `accounts` row expects. `"evidence"` is the evidence repository
749 < 1   (the operator's `popmechanic/fleet-evidence`); `--evidence-repo` overrides it per launch, and a
750 < 1   launch with neither is refused. A key outside those four is a key nothing reads: the `capacity`
751 < 1   row is red and names it.
752 < 1 - **Logs without an env var:** `ssh <ssh_dest> 'journalctl _SYSTEMD_USER_UNIT=fleet-run@<N>.service --no-pager -n 200'`
753 < 1   reads the run unit's journal by field match, so it needs no `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` and no `--user`. The
754 < 1   setup script's own output is `~/fleet-setup.log` on the VM.
755 < 1 - **Lobby errors:** every lobby call captures stdout+stderr; on non-zero exit the tool prints ALL of it
756 < 1   verbatim (`exe.dev <verb> failed (exit N):\n<output>`) — no envelope is documented.
757 < 1 - **Naming for exe.dev verbs:** every lobby verb, every `git` and every `gh` command runs through the
758 < 1   module's `exec` seam so tests stub them; every value interpolated into a lobby string passes
759 < 1   `isSafeTarget`, `isFullSha`, `isRunNumber` or `isVmName` first. Never a `--cmds` lobby key on any VM.
760 < 1 - **Facts (measured 2026-09-03, Shelley's rig + our probes):** (1) exe.dev's GitHub edge routes each
761 < 1   request BY REPO PATH and serves a cached installation token for ~30–60 s after an integration is
762 < 1   edited — which is why the run's integration reaches the VM by a standing tag attachment from creation and
763 < 1   is never swapped in at publish time; (2) two GitHub integrations naming the same repo attached to one VM have
764 < 1   no documented tie-break; (3) the aggregate host proxies only `/repos/OWNER/REPO/...`
765 < 1   (`/user` → edge 403), so `gh auth status`/`gh api user` can never work through it and are not
766 < 1   health checks.
767 < 1 
768 < 1 ## Rules
769 < 1 - Amendment 10: models never run git; every git command and every GitHub call is a script's.
770 < 1 - No secret on any VM and none in any argv. The Claude bearer reaches the edge on stdin only.
771 < 1 - Scripts pass `bash -n`; tests: pytest under `tests/`, node `.mjs` under `fleet/tests/` (sentinel `ALL
772 < 1   TESTS PASSED`, 300 s per file, no network, stub `curl`/`git`/`gh`/`ssh`/`systemd-run`/`systemctl` via a PATH shim).
773 < 1   Test behaviour, not sentences; no test pins a sentence of a document.
774 < 1 - Prefer deleting to adapting. A file named for what it does.
775 < 1 